						<tr>
							<td height="50" colspan="3" valign="top" class="windowbg2" align="left">It&#039;s a little overdue, but I just wanted to issue an apology on behalf of myself and Saba to everybody who came to the August 30, 2007 show in Bend, Oregon to watch us open for Matisyahu. It&#039;s the first time we&#039;ve ever straight-up missed a tourdate like that and hopefully the last for a real long time. Beyond any personal or physical limitations, there really are no rationalizations for missing a show, but the best I can do is offer a little explanation to dispel any rumors that Saba and I were too busy snorting coke or that we loathe the good city of Bend (because we don&#039;t -&nbsp; in fact, we dig Bend... especially our good folkers at The Grove!). There&#039;s also a rumor that we canceled because I don&#039;t agree with the Zionism that Matisyahu promotes through his music. That certainly isn&#039;t the reason we didn&#039;t do the show, but I&#039;ll say (as always)... Free Palestine and end the occupation!<br /><br />Truth is, we got up late and missed our flight from Las Vegas to Seattle (and consequently, Seattle to Bend). By about 30 seconds. Literally. We arrived in time to check-in and were on our way to the gate when the lady at the counter changed her mind and decided it was too late and that we&#039;d have to take the next flight. We argued to no avail. There were no flights that would take us to Bend before 9pm. So we had to cancel that morning and take an L for this one.<br /><br />Again, apologies to all who came thru expecting to see us, only to find out that we canceled. Especially those of yall who made a long drive to Bend. Keep those ticket stubs - we&#039;ll get you back somehow. So stay tuned, right here!<br /><br />Peace<br />Geo<br /><br /><br /><br /><br /><br /><br /></td>
						</tr>
